# Rudder spanwise parametrisation, one station per row, root first
# source   : Wind_Tunnel_Rudder.stp
# frame    : origin at the root leading edge; +X LE->TE, +Y root->tip, +Z thickness
# units    : lengths mm, angles deg, shape parameters / chord
# sweep and dihedral: 'cumulative' is measured from the spanwise vertical through the
#            root reference point to the line joining it to that station's reference
#            point; 'local' is the tangent, d(offset)/d(span). Equal for a straight edge.
# twist    : angle of the section chord line, positive nose-up (LE on the +Z side)
# tilt     : slope of the chord line in the span direction, from the LE and TE heights:
#            tilt_ratio = (y_te - y) / (x_te - x_le), tilt = arctan(tilt_ratio), positive TE up.
#            In the XCAD file (height along z) these are z1 and z2 of the LE and TE.
# rows     : 201, y = 0.000000 up to 200.000000 mm
# tip      : the last row is the tilted tip section, top of the LE to top of the TE,
#            tilt 3.576626 deg (ratio 0.062505103); every other row is horizontal, tilt 0.
#            Its chord, twist and shape are those of its own airfoil, measured untilted;
#            its reference points sit at their own heights. The fits and the planform
#            summary use the horizontal rows only, and the local (tangent) columns are NaN
#            on the tilted row. Its tilt is a design variable for the optimisation stage.
# cap      : the tip cap above the tilted section (Step 7, tip_cap.py): face 0.6167 -> 2.9939 mm,
#            crown radius 59.198 mm, edge radius 0.7070 mm, TE corner radius 3.2949 mm;
#            fit to 0.1163 mm max, 0.0427 mm rms. Details in parameters.json and cap_profile.dat.
# load     : np.loadtxt(path)  -> (201, 26)
#
# columns
#    1  y                [ mm]  station height above the root
#    2  eta              [  -]  y / span
#    3  chord            [ mm]  true LE->TE length in the section plane
#    4  chord_x          [ mm]  chordwise projection of the chord
#    5  x_le             [ mm]  leading-edge x
#    6  z_le             [ mm]  leading-edge z
#    7  x_te             [ mm]  trailing-edge x
#    8  z_te             [ mm]  trailing-edge z
#    9  sweep_le         [deg]  cumulative LE sweep from the root LE, positive aft
#   10  sweep_c4         [deg]  cumulative quarter-chord sweep, positive aft
#   11  sweep_c2         [deg]  cumulative mid-chord sweep, positive aft
#   12  sweep_te         [deg]  cumulative TE sweep, positive aft
#   13  sweep_le_local   [deg]  local LE sweep, d(x_le)/d(span)
#   14  sweep_c4_local   [deg]  local quarter-chord sweep
#   15  rake             [ mm]  LE offset out of the planform plane (propeller rake)
#   16  dihedral         [deg]  cumulative dihedral / rake angle, positive toward +Z
#   17  dihedral_local   [deg]  local dihedral angle
#   18  twist            [deg]  section twist / pitch angle, positive nose-up
#   19  t_over_c         [  -]  maximum thickness / chord
#   20  x_tmax           [  -]  x/c of maximum thickness
#   21  camber           [  -]  maximum camber / chord, signed
#   22  x_cmax           [  -]  x/c of maximum camber, NaN on a symmetric section
#   23  r_le             [  -]  leading-edge radius / chord
#   24  y_te             [ mm]  trailing-edge height; equal to y except on the tilted tip section
#   25  tilt_ratio       [  -]  (y_te - y) / (x_te - x_le), rise of the chord line over its run
#   26  tilt             [deg]  section tilt about the thickness axis, arctan(tilt_ratio), positive TE up
#
# fitted form of each distribution
#   chord            linear                 mean +159.145163  spread 2.114e+01
#   chord_x          linear                 mean +159.145163  spread 2.114e+01
#   x_le             linear                 mean +6.982456  spread 6.982e+00
#   z_le             constant               mean -0.000000  spread 2.857e-14
